## 2. Stack & design choices

### Stack Choice

I chose HTML, CSS, and JavaScript because I am already familiar with them and felt confident using them for a smaller frontend project like this. Frontend development is not my main area of focus since I am more interested in data engineering, so I preferred using technologies I already understood instead of spending time learning a larger framework for a relatively simple application.

### Design Decision 1 — Minimalist layout

I intentionally kept the UI very minimal to reduce distractions and keep the focus on the timer itself. Since a Pomodoro timer is meant to help concentration, I wanted the interface to feel clean and uncluttered instead of overloaded with features or panels.

### Design Decision 2 — Large centered timer

I made the timer extremely large and placed it in the center of the screen so it becomes the main visual element of the application. The large typography makes it readable at a glance and gives the app a stronger visual identity. I also added different glow colors for focus and break states to make the current mode instantly recognizable.

