## 3. Responsive & accessibility

### Responsive behavior

The layout of the website is intentionally simple, so it behaves similarly across both mobile and desktop devices. I tested the application on multiple screen resolutions to ensure the timer, buttons, and sliding session panel remain usable and properly aligned on smaller screens as well as larger desktop displays.

### Accessibility consideration handled

One accessibility consideration I handled was visual clarity. I used large typography, strong contrast between text and background, and clear visual indicators for focus and break states so the timer is easy to read and understand quickly.

### Accessibility consideration skipped

I did not fully implement advanced accessibility features such as screen reader support, ARIA labels, or complete keyboard-only navigation. With more time, I would improve accessibility support further and test the application using accessibility auditing tools.

