## 4. AI usage

### AI tools used

I used the built-in VS Code AI assistant with Claude Haiku as the main model.

### What AI helped with

AI assisted with nearly the entire development process, including:

- Timer functionality
- UI generation
- Styling ideas
- Session history functionality
- localStorage persistence
- Responsive layout adjustments
- General debugging and refinement

Since it had been a long time since I last built a website, I relied heavily on AI-assisted development throughout the project.

### Changes made to AI-generated output

The initial version generated by AI was functional but visually very basic, and the session history feature was not working correctly. I improved the overall UI direction to make the app feel more premium and visually focused.

I also manually adjusted several styling details myself, including:
- Increasing the font size of the central timer
- Reducing button sizes for better visual balance
- Fixing margins and spacing issues in the CSS

These smaller refinements helped improve the overall appearance and usability of the application.

---

## 5. Honest gap

The main area that could still be improved is the visual design polish. The overall functionality of the project is intentionally simple, but I think the final quality of this type of application depends heavily on presentation and interaction design.

With another day of work, I would spend more time improving the visual design system, animations, transitions, and theme customization. I would especially like to add multiple themes similar to websites like Monkeytype to make the application feel more dynamic and personalized.
